    {
      "id": "claim_d82f88f3daa04efeacd6ef5092f8d56e",
      "statement": "Every agent/reviewer run trigger (Slack, Linear, GitHub, dashboard, scheduler) routes through a single durable dispatch contract, openswe/dispatch.py:dispatch_agent_run, which selects the graph via assistant_id ('agent' or 'reviewer') and treats source as metadata/logging only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/dispatch.py#L429-L467",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6440c64c4a078a0f6a8c80cb0ae83af130ecc9a6d9b15bef187600010b61d901:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_45387ab772f3437e9c3a2030f69732d5",
      "statement": "The dispatch contract defaults to multitask_strategy='interrupt' (a follow-up halts and resumes the active run with full history plus the new message), durability='async' checkpointing before each step written while the next step runs, stream_resumable=False (streams not retained in the platform), and v3 protocol markers so the dashboard can observe runs from transcript context without replay. Background work may explicitly choose another multitask strategy such as 'enqueue'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/dispatch.py#L1-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:61d058b2bde0ae1164ea4175a95f41a2c741a5d8332fad1d940657ee004b508b:"
        },
        {
